    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λημ-άω</span></b> , only pres., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήμη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be bleared</i>, of the eyes, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				2.18
			</span></i>; <i>to be blear-eyed</i> or <i>purblind</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λημᾶν κολοκύνταις</span>
			<i>to have one's eyes running</i> pumpkins, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				327
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. καὶ ἀμβλυώττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονικαῖς λήμαις λ. τὰς φρένας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					581
				</span></i>
			.</div>
